te":"2014-10-07T12:48:03-07:00","id":274937,"title":"","content":"I haven't played it yet, but in my understanding, Shadow of Mordor protagonist seem to have something like a Geist helping him. I believe the wraith even revived him, or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/196-max-deltree","name":"Max Deltree","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar196_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-07T15:41:12-07:00","id":275024,"title":"","content":"If we're on about computer games, anyone remember Clock Tower 3 on the PS2? Then you got the Fatal Frame series, F.E.A.R series and the Silent Hill series.<br /> <br /> Recently, Murdered: Soul Suspect is based around ghosty stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-16T13:11:34-07:00","id":284104,"title":"","content":"The anime <i>Noragami</i> looks like it has promise as well for fans of Geist. It's made by Bones, the studio behind <i>Cowboy Bebop</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Hiyori Iki was a regular middle school student until she was hit by a bus while trying to save the life of a jersey-wearing person named Yato. This incident causes her to transform into a half-phantom. Soon after she learns that Yato is a god, her life is never going to be the same again. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/36-tomewilson","name":"tomewilson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar36_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-16T15:19:36-07:00","id":284273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tomewilson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/256390-sources-of-inspiration-for-geist?p=284104#post284104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The anime <i>Noragami</i> looks like it has promise as well for fans of Geist. It's made by Bones, the studio behind <i>Cowboy Bebop</i>.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I remember thinking Rabo's invocation prior to absorbing a Storm was particularly resonant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 06-07-2015, 07:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-21T09:57:54-07:00","id":288648,"title":"","content":"The webcomic <a href=\"http://avasdemon.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Ava's Demon</a> is basically &quot;Alien Geists in Space&quot;. I can't say much more without setting spoilers (what I just said was already quite spoilery), but the parallels are extensive (also the art is gorgeous, just go read it)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/996-gabby","name":"Gabby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-21T15:29:41-07:00","id":288997,"title":"","content":"What Gabby said. I only hope the artist/writer gets better soon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T19:13:03-08:00","id":424750,"title":"","content":"Thank you for your recommendations. I just saw &quot;JoJo's Bizarre Adventure: Stardust Crusade&quot; for the first time. Quite an interesting take on qeists. I can't believe I forgot about ParaNorman and Beetlejuice. The giant metallic eyeball thing at the end of the Persona 4 anime would make a good Cthonian adversary. I've got to use Potterville from the 2nd episode of &quot;Over The Garden Wall&quot; as part of my underworld landscape. I haven't gotten a copy of Shadow of Mordor yet but It is definitely on my wish list.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1869-moonwolf8","name":"moonwolf8","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T19:54:00-08:00","id":424786,"title":"","content":"I second Jacob's Latter, not only for the Demons/Angel thingies and their appearances (for Geists and Ghosts) but also Jacob for being an example of how fresh ghosts would be like in mindset and the whole process of letting go from their perspective (for the cognizant ones anyway).<br /> <br /> John Dies at the End Movie and Book, both for the nightmare imagery and the blas\u00e9 fare attitude John and Dave have over everything, the Movie for showing (in my mind atleast) what the supernatural masquerade would actually look like in NWoD and the importance of supernatural sensing abilities. The book because the movie dropped the most important twist and is fundamentally tied to the beginning I won't say what for spoiler purposes but I think it is relevant to NWoD in general.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2111-doeman","name":"DoeMan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T22:04:21-08:00","id":424895,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/256390-sources-of-inspiration-for-geist?p=264136#post264136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fades; great but sadly short lived BBC tv series.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was under the impression that The Fades ended exactly where it was meant to.<br /> <br /> But yeah, it's a good one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5158-xenu-s-paradox","name":"Xenu's Paradox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-04T09:42:40-08:00","id":427794,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://www.telegraph.co.uk/news/worldnews/europe/france/11442043/200-bodies-found-in-mass-grave-beneath-Paris-supermarket.html\" target=\"_blank\">Incidentally, a mass grave was recently discovered beneath a Parisian supermarket.</a><br /> <br /> This sort of event could be a cool catalyst for a Geist story. In the World of Darkness, maybe this is a much more regular occurrence.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-15T17:07:07-07:00","id":443315,"title":"","content":"Seconding Jojo's Bizarre Adventure. Every time I think about the Rage manifestation I mentally hear &quot;ORAORAORAORAORAORAORAORAORAORAORA!&quot;<br /> <br /> And Persona 3 is even listed as an inspiration in the book. Also, the Persona games provide a lot of reference photos for Geists, while the soundtrack is perfect for Geist (and a lot of other WoD games).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T02:29:26-07:00","id":443949,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DoeMan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/256390-sources-of-inspiration-for-geist?p=424786#post424786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I second Jacob's Latter, not only for the Demons/Angel thingies and their appearances (for Geists and Ghosts) but also Jacob for being an example of how fresh ghosts would be like in mindset and the whole process of letting go from their perspective (for the cognizant ones anyway).<br /> <br /> John Dies at the End Movie and Book, both for the nightmare imagery and the blas\u00e9 fare attitude John and Dave have over everything, the Movie for showing (in my mind atleast) what the supernatural masquerade would actually look like in NWoD and the importance of supernatural sensing abilities. The book because the movie dropped the most important twist and is fundamentally tied to the beginning I won't say what for spoiler purposes but I think it is relevant to NWoD in general.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll agree with John Dies at the End... I think it works with nwod in general myself, looking back seeing Korrok as a manifestation of the God-Machine, for example.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T16:19:11-07:00","id":445052,"title":"","content":"<i>Paranorman</i> is a beautiful little film about a young medium who's powers leave him isolated from those around him, and is a wonderful basis for a marginally lighter Geist story","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-18T14:42:18-07:00","id":518439,"title":"","content":"Time for some (very appropriate) thread necromancy.<br /> <br /> Death Vigil, a comic by Stjepan Sejic<span style=\"font-family:Arial, sans-serif\"> published by TopCow/Image is an amazing Geist reference. The main characters are literally people who die and make a deal with a death entity (in this case, its all the same one, the Grim Reaper herself) to comeback to life and gain powers from it.<br /> <br /> And... the first 7(!) issues are free right now on Stjepan's DeviantArt: </span>http://nebezial.deviantart.com/gallery/47267490/death-vigil<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial, sans-serif\">You can also preo-order the first volume from Amazon right now: </span>http://www.amazon.com/Death-Vigil-Volume-Stjepan-Sejic/dp/1632152789<br /> <br /> Just a warning, some of his other work on DeviantArt is NSFW, but Death Vigil itself is fine.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-19T10:43:49-07:00","id":519743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/256390-sources-of-inspiration-for-geist?p=443315#post443315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seconding Jojo's Bizarre Adventure. Every time I think about the Rage manifestation I mentally hear &quot;ORAORAORAORAORAORAORAORAORAORAORA!&quot;<br /> <br /> And Persona 3 is even listed as an inspiration in the book. Also, the Persona games provide a lot of reference photos for Geists, while the soundtrack is perfect for Geist (and a lot of other WoD games).</div> </div> </div> </div>Thirding Jojo, especially the later parts (Part 4+). Stands are similar in many ways to Geister, Stand users gather in Krewes, solve mysteries often involving ghosts, souls, and the undead, and employ weird modern (body)horror abilities that are each a miniature mystery in its own right. It's easy to write off Jojo as weird camp, but it still manages an impressive balance of horror, action, and mystery.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T16:20:50-07:00","id":544457,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/256390-sources-of-inspiration-for-geist?p=518439#post518439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Time for some (very appropriate) thread necromancy.<br /> <br /> Death Vigil, a comic by Stjepan Sejic<span style=\"font-family:Arial, sans-serif\"> published by TopCow/Image is an amazing Geist reference. The main characters are literally people who die and make a deal with a death entity (in this case, its all the same one, the Grim Reaper herself) to comeback to life and gain powers from it.<br /> <br /> And... the first 7(!) issues are free right now on Stjepan's DeviantArt: </span>http://nebezial.deviantart.com/gallery/47267490/death-vigil<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial, sans-serif\">You can also preo-order the first volume from Amazon right now: </span>http://www.amazon.com/Death-Vigil-Volume-Stjepan-Sejic/dp/1632152789<br /> <br /> Just a warning, some of his other work on DeviantArt is NSFW, but Death Vigil itself is fine.</div> </div> </div> </div>I may need to check this out, I've seen it and looked at the odd preview... As my pull-list empties as miniseries end, I may pick this up. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T23:26:14-07:00","id":546576,"title":"","content":"The anime series <u><b><i>Bleach</i></b></u> and <u><i><b>Soul Eater</b></i></u> are both death/afterlife/ghost themed stories that focus on characters with supernatural powers as a result of some form of symbiotic relationship.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-13T14:12:40-07:00","id":700118,"title":"","content":"These lyrics from &quot;Jesus Christ Superstar&quot; kind of remind me of how it might feel to be tormented by needy ghosts.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> Jesus: My time is almost through<br /> Little left to do<br /> After all, I've tried for three years<br /> Seems like thirty, seems like thirty<br /> <br /> Crowd:<br /> See my eyes, I can hardly see<br /> See me stand, I can hardly walk<br /> I believe you can make me whole<br /> See my tongue, I can hardly talk<br /> See my skin, I'm a mass of blood<br /> See my legs, I can hardly stand<br /> I believe you can make me well<br /> See my purse, I'm a poor, poor man<br /> Will you touch, will you mend me Christ?<br /> Won't you touch, will you heal me Christ?<br /> Will you kiss, you can cure me Christ<br /> Won't you kiss, won't you pay me Christ?<br /> See my eyes, I can hardly see<br /> See me stand, I can hardly walk<br /> I believe you can make me whole<br /> See my tongue, I can hardly talk<br /> See my skin, I'm a mass of blood<br /> See my legs, I can hardly stand<br /> I believe you can make me well<br /> See my purse, I'm a poor, poor man<br /> Will you touch, will you mend me Christ?<br /> Won't you touch, will you heal me Christ?<br /> Will you kiss, can you cure me Christ?<br /> Won't you kiss, won't you pay me Christ?<br /> See my eyes, I can hardly see<br /> See me stand, I can hardly walk<br /> I believe you can make me whole<br /> See my tongue, I can hardly talk<br /> See my skin, I'm a mass of blood<br /> See my legs, I can hardly stand<br /> I believe you can make me well<br /> See my purse, I'm a poor, poor man<br /> Will you touch, will you mend me Christ?<br /> Won't you touch, will you heal me Christ?<br /> Will you kiss, can you cure me Christ?<br /> Won't you kiss, won't you pay me Christ?<br /> <br /> Jesus<br /> Ooo, there's too many of you<br /> Don't push me<br /> Oh, there's too little of me<br /> Don't, don't crowd me, please don't crowd me<br /> Oh, heal yourselves<br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><br /> Read more: <a href=\"http://www.metrolyrics.com/the-temple-lyrics-jesus-christ-superstar.html#ixzz3oU6ouENl\" target=\"_blank\">Jesus Christ Superstar - The Temple Lyrics | MetroLyrics</a></span></div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2015-inspectorjavert","name":"inspectorjavert","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-13T14:19:48-07:00","id":700121,"title":"","content":"As the book says the <i>Final Destination </i>movies are great fodder: the deaths in them are tailor made for The Forgotten. Further they seem to give an idea of what some people might be like before the bargain in that one character *spoiler* always seems to have some precognition before the accident. I think the idea of Death and its nature are lost in the later movies (after 2) in favor of more gore and T &amp; A.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2015-inspectorjavert","name":"inspectorjavert","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-14T08:57:46-07:00","id":700942,"title":"","content":"For those who were interested, the Trade Paperback of Death Vigil should be in Comic Stores today and ship from Amazon soon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T08:03:06-07:00","id":741792,"title":"","content":"&quot;Shadow of Mordor&quot; is very much like Geist. When you die in the game, you don't just reload at the last checkpoint, time actually passes in the game world before the Wraith resurrects you again. Sound familiar?<br /> <br /> For a movie, &quot;Odd Thomas&quot; is a lot better than the title would suggest. It definitely made me want to read the books it's based on (haven't gotten around to it yet).<br /> <br /> Since others have suggested anime, I'll point this out: in &quot;Fullmetal Alchemist: Brotherhood,&quot; the dynamic betwween Ling and Greed reminds me a lot of how a Geist and its Sin-Eater would interact.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2573-inkpenavenger","name":"inkpenavenger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2573_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T13:12:19-07:00","id":742645,"title":"","content":"Spawn <br /> Shin Megami Tensei: Persona<br /> Middle-Earth: Shadow of Mordor<br /> The Darkness comic, and games<br /> Marvel Spiderman's Symbiot characters<br /> Bleach maybe? The swords have identities<br /> Soul Eater<br /> Shaman King","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-27T02:15:53-08:00","id":1162935,"title":"","content":"I came to this thread a few years ago to get inspiration for my first sin eater game and now, having created several long running storys that were well received by my players, I think the greatest inspirations for this gameline for me was horrific world news made sensible by the gallows humor of philosophers like Neitzsche and Seneca.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6516-mefathiel8","name":"mefathiel8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6516_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-27T11:33:19-08:00","id":1163072,"title":"","content":"Tim Burton's <i>The Corpse Bride </i>seems very Geisty to me. Probably because its a lovely little ghost story. Perhaps the Land of the Dead is a bit too upbeat for a Dead Dominion, but there are arcane rules you have to follow even there. You could even see the Corpse Bride as a Geist who would have bonded with Victor had he finished the deadly wedding ritual.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-06T19:04:29-08:00","id":1165732,"title":"","content":"Abattoir works as an amazing story. I won't lay out any spoilers here, however, I have borrowed HEAVILY from this in an ongoing Geist game. The players seem to enjoy it a lot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Kinda I want to&quot; - Trent Reznor<br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://scontent.ftpa1-2.fna.fbcdn.net/v/t1.0-9/27973518_2040009129348529_5319855605701568493_n.jpg?oh=9c85c5c9d4a0769a1249ea2f3e62ca43&amp;oe=5B002AA5\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12143-eldritchminister","name":"EldritchMinister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12143_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-22T08:23:04-07:00","id":1210032,"title":"","content":"In volume 5 of Twin Star Exorcists it is revealed that exorcists get their power from the spirits of a dead exorcist. I don't know if they go over this in the anime or not, I've only gotten up to episode 35 so far.<br /> <br /> \u200bmefathiel8 can you give us some quotes of Nietzsche and Seneca that have helped frame World events for you?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1869-moonwolf8","name":"moonwolf8","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-22T08:35:50-07:00","id":1210038,"title":"","content":"The game <i>Beyond: Two Souls </i>comes to mind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-23T10:54:28-07:00","id":1221502,"title":"","content":"The Abhorsen series by Garth Nix could work well, especially for Gatekeepers. The series follows a sect of necromancers dedicated not to raising zombies, but maintaining the balance between the living and the dead.<br /> <br /> Lupe Fiasco's The Cool could also be interpreted as a Geist story, with Michael Young History being the Bound and The Game being a Geist. Then again, this being The Cool, it can be interpreted to mean near about *anything*.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24176,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24176-borne","user":"Borne","date":". 05-23-2018, 04:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24176-borne","name":"Borne","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24176_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-24T19:20:12-07:00","id":1221914,"title":"","content":"Evil Dead for antagonists is always fun and many Sin Eaters do end up dealing with some occultist experiment gone horribly wrong. Cemetery Man is another good one if you want a decent depiction of what a Gatekeeper Sin Eater gets up to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24168-madman777","name":"Madman777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-24T21:24:12-07:00","id":1221938,"title":"","content":"One I don't think I've seen: the Greywalker series of Urban Fantasy novels by Kat Richardson. I never finished the series, unfortunately, but they involve a detective who dies and comes back able to see &quot;the Grey,&quot; the world that ghosts seem to inhabit, and even enter it partially. There are a few other powers that are reminiscent of a Sin Eater as well that are a bit spoilery.<br /> <br /> Also, Mike Carey's Felix Castor novels have a lot of focus on ghosts, making them ultimately responsible for just about every supernatural thing except demons (which are another matter entirely). Vampires, zombies, and werebeasts are all the result of undead spirits inhabiting various physical forms.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1407-endlesskng","name":"EndlessKng","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-26T02:29:07-07:00","id":1222190,"title":"","content":"I can't watch the History, Discovery, or Travel channels anymore without seeing potential cenotes, Haunts (1e vernacular, can't get my head around the new terms), and Avernian Gates everywhere. From the Nazca water funnels with their deep aquifers to the Puerta de Hayu Marca to the ritual chamber underneath the Pyramid of the Feathered Serpent with its miniature scale model &quot;Underworld&quot; and liquid mercury channels, there are some great mysterious locations out there in the world. Even Ancient Aliens features a lot of &quot;mystical&quot; places from ancient civilizations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/2.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12708-chesh","name":"Chesh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12708_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-26T04:40:45-07:00","id":1222208,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chesh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/256390-sources-of-inspiration-for-geist?p=1222190#post1222190\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Haunts (1e vernacular, can't get my head around the new terms)</div> </div> </div> </div>We haven't got a replacement term for Haunt yet, so you're in the clear.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-26T07:53:49-07:00","id":1222248,"title":"","content":"Actually, the topic of Avernian Gates reminds me of Rick Riordan's novels, especially Heroes of Olympus - the fourth book is called &quot;The House of Hades&quot; and deals with having to find the titular structure and close the doors to the Underworld. Might be an idea for an inspiration for an Avernian Gate. That book also has some interesting investigation of the Underworld as well.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1407-endlesskng","name":"EndlessKng","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-30T05:02:28-07:00","id":1223165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EndlessKng</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/256390-sources-of-inspiration-for-geist?p=1222248#post1222248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue ani